# 8. The “Frozen Model” is methodologically very important

The document at 12:27 makes a distinction that I consider excellent:

| Status   | Meaning                             |
| -------- | ----------------------------------- |
| BASELINE | theory experiments run against      |
| FROZEN   | question closed in its present form |
| PROPOSED | candidate not adopted               |

Most importantly:

$$
\boxed{\text{Freezing}\neq\text{Promotion}}
$$

A frozen negative result remains negative. A frozen result can be cited or explicitly reopened, but should not be silently revised. 

This is exactly the kind of **epistemic version control** the programme needs.

