# 9. The “N_eff” failure is actually a methodological success

The frozen result is particularly valuable because it prevents the programme from endlessly hunting for a magic complexity formula.

The evidence shows:

* tolerance relation may be non-transitive;
* quotient construction can therefore fail;
* packing avoids the transitivity problem;
* packing nevertheless fails to capture dependence;
* pairwise distinguishability is insufficient for family-level behaviour.



So we now have a useful three-level distinction:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Identity}
\rightarrow
\text{Pairwise distinguishability}
\rightarrow
\text{Joint family behaviour}
}
$$

with different mathematical questions at each level. 

This should **not** be collapsed into one equivalence relation.

